WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 32 Student Video
Unit 8, Lesson 4: Challenges

1
00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:18.290
Years ago, our family became friends with another young family in our neighborhood.

2
00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:22.970
The kids were about the same age as our kids and the mom and dad had a lot in common

3
00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:27.490
with my wife and I. Well, as we got to know him, it was very clear that the father

4
00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:31.170
who became a good friend of mine was not a Christian.

5
00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:34.410
In fact, we had conversations about heaven and hell.

6
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:39.830
We had conversations about the scientific evidence for God and he was the consummate

7
00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:41.490
skeptic. He always had a way out or a question or a

8
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:50.010
way of avoiding the evidence. And then years later, they ended up moving to the Northwest.

9
00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.550
And when I heard that they were going to move, I had a couple of thoughts.

10
00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:58.090
I thought, well, number one, gosh, he's no longer going to have me in his life and

11
00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:01.150
other Christian friends in our neighborhood to talk to him about God.

12
00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:05.910
And he's such a skeptic. He's never going to believe.

13
00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:11.990
But then sometime later I started noticing he was posting quotes by C.S. Lewis

14
00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:16.730
on social media. He was posting these Christian ideas.

15
00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:21.850
To make a long story short, a few summers ago I had a chance to go up the Northwest

16
00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:25.710
and baptize him because he'd become a Christian.

17
00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:30.250
And on that same day his young son was baptized as well.

18
00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:34.150
It was truly one of the most amazing experiences of my life.

19
00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:39.850
I think there's four principles we can learn from this experience first

20
00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:45.750
for many people coming to faith can take a long time sometimes even years

21
00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:51.690
many people have emotional intellectual moral and relational issues to work

22
00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:57.030
through this is certainly true for my friend before they can consider the claims of

23
00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:02.730
christ second sometimes people are at a point in their lives where they're just not

24
00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:08.310
open to faith. Even people walked away from Jesus in the flesh.

25
00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:13.210
Years ago, when my friend was still skeptic, I had him speak into a group of my high

26
00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:16.070
school students and I was trying to teach my students how do you have genuine

27
00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:18.810
conversations with people who see the world differently?

28
00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:22.070
And in the middle of this conversation, my friend said to my students, he said,

29
00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:25.190
look, if your teacher Sean could give me evidence, I would believe.

30
00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:29.670
I just don't see the evidence. And then in the conversation later, somehow it

31
00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:33.550
shifted. I don't remember how, but somehow the group was talking about the

32
00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:38.590
legalization of marijuana and my friend says he goes look the bottom line is I just

33
00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:42.610
don't want the government coming into my house telling me how to live it's my house

34
00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:46.590
and I stopped him I said wait a minute a minute ago you said you'd follow the

35
00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:51.530
evidence now I think you have the answer why you don't you know Jesus says I stand

36
00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:56.950
at the door and knock he's the ultimate governing authority God wants to come into

37
00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:01.490
your house and tell you how to live you didn't want the government to tell you

38
00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:05.810
whether you could smoke marijuana or not maybe the real issue is you just don't want

39
00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:09.250
God in your life telling you how to live he looked at me and he says I don't

40
00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:13.690
understand I tried three times to explain it and I gave up do you know years later when

41
00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:17.430
he became a Christian he pointed back to that and he said Sean you were right it

42
00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:23.410
wasn't a lack of evidence I simply did not want an authority in my life telling me

43
00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:28.470
how to live friends sometimes people are not at a point in their life for a variety

44
00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:34.250
of reasons to even be open to issues of faith third my friend

45
00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:39.790
shared with me that back when he was a skeptic he had doubts about his faith now we

46
00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:43.810
just talked about doubt and sometimes we tend to think that it's only christians who

47
00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:49.430
have doubts but that's not true people of all walks of life and different beliefs

48
00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:54.910
often have doubts my friend would go to sleep at night sometimes and wonder

49
00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:58.470
is there really anything to this claim about God?

50
00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.250
What if I'm wrong about my skeptical beliefs?

51
00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:07.530
So the challenge for us is to ask the right questions to get people to doubt their

52
00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.790
skeptical beliefs and hopefully come to Christ.

53
00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:15.430
And fourth, relationships really matter.

54
00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:20.450
It was certainly truth that was important in my friend's journey, but it was also

55
00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:25.950
the love and relationship of believers that drew him in when his heart was open.

56
00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:31.470
We've talked a lot in this study about how important it is to speak truth, but to do

57
00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:36.330
it in a loving fashion. Jesus came in grace and he came in truth.

58
00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:41.350
Yes, we need to speak truth, but from a heart of love and a heart of compassion.

59
00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:47.010
In fact, we need to be willing to love people because they're made in the image of

60
00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:50.390
God even if they never come to faith.

61
00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:57.190
We have been on a long journey together.

62
00:04:57.470 --> 00:05:01.410
We started by looking at the relationship between faith and reason and exploring

63
00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:06.570
questions of truth. And then we looked at some different worldviews, pantheism,

64
00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:12.610
naturalism, and monotheism. Then we considered the scientific evidence from DNA and

65
00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:16.270
fine-tuning pointing towards an intelligent designer.

66
00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:21.610
And then after that, we looked at these signposts that point towards purpose in the

67
00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:27.530
universe beauty morality free will and story and then we examine the

68
00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:33.270
specific historical evidence for jesus and for the reliability of the bible and then

69
00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:38.390
after that we considered some of the biggest objections to the faith hell and evil

70
00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:44.370
and in this final unit we've asked the question what now do you

71
00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:48.790
have all your questions answered probably not in fact you might even have more

72
00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:54.070
questions now than when we started but i want to impress something very important

73
00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:59.950
upon you and it's this that you are ready you've been trained well i had a public

74
00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:04.730
debate some years ago and i called up one of my professors from grad school and as

75
00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:08.150
we were talking about it he said something to me i'll never forget he said sean

76
00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:13.730
you've been trained well and the same is true for you you will always have

77
00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:18.670
questions there's always new issues that arise But you have learned truth well and

78
00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:23.310
you are ready if you put your training into practice to engage family and friends

79
00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:27.370
and others of our non-believing world with the gospel.

80
00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:28.510
You're ready.

81
00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:35.030
Not only are you ready, but God wants you to step out boldly and put this training

82
00:06:35.030 --> 00:06:39.910
into practice. You maybe have heard it said that with great power comes great

83
00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:43.030
responsibility. This is actually a biblical idea.

84
00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:47.310
Jesus said he who has been given much, much is required.

85
00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:52.010
You've been blessed by people who care enough about you to take you through this

86
00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:55.590
training. The question is what will you do with it?

87
00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:02.550
God wants you to speak truth boldly and yet He wants you to do it with a heart of

88
00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:05.790
love. He wants you to speak truth with compassion.

89
00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:12.030
Friends we live in a broken and a hurting world that desperately needs Jesus.

90
00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:18.050
We live in a world that desperately needs people to speak the truth about Jesus, the

91
00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:20.310
only truth that can set people free.

92
00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:23.430
The question is will that be you?

